      "writtenOn": "2019-06-11T11:45:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry I just wrote that as an example but had not checked it at all. I don\u0027t think this is actually the right test.\n\nTo do things well, I think probably the right test would be something like this :\nOne of : VERIFYING_POOR_LINK, CAPTIVE_PORTAL_CHECK, CONNECTED, SUSPENDED, BLOCKED\n\nBut I think it\u0027s also fine (and maybe better, especially considering all these states are deprecated) to say something like this :\n\n  // VPNs can only ever send the IDLE, CONNECTING, CONNECTED, DISCONNECTED or FAILED detailed states.\n  // A VPN is not in force if it\u0027s in IDLE, DISCONNECTED or FAILED detailed status (they all map\n  // to the DISCONNECTED status). It\u0027s also not yet in force if CONNECTING.\n  // Therefore, a VPN is only ever in force when its state is CONNECTED.\n  return state \u003d\u003d DetailedState.CONNECTED;\n\nI just checked that this should be accurate, so if you agree this is better then let\u0027s just use this.\n(you may simplify the second, third and fourth sentences to to \"Out of these, the VPN is only in force when CONNECTED.\" if you prefer that)",
